<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>PrompTugal: do it yourself</title>
<meta name="description" content="Everything that runs PrompTugal.news is open source. The repositories, the stack, the roadmap in ten steps, the lessons we paid for, and what it actually takes: fork it, or build it with us. Investor deck 8, November 2026.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="deck.css">
<style>
/* deck 8 only */
code, .code { font: 400 21px/1.35 var(--mono); color: var(--ink); background: var(--paper-2); padding: 2px 8px; }
.slide.ink code { background: #2a2b31; color: var(--paper); }
.steps5 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 22px; margin-top: 40px; }
.steps5 .s { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--hair); border-top: 8px solid var(--green); padding: 24px 22px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
.steps5 .s.c { border-top-color: var(--cobalt); } .steps5 .s.r { border-top-color: var(--red); } .steps5 .s.k { border-top-color: var(--ink); }
.steps5 .s .n { font: 600 58px/1 var(--serif); color: var(--green); }
.steps5 .s.c .n { color: var(--cobalt); } .steps5 .s.r .n { color: var(--red); } .steps5 .s.k .n { color: var(--ink); }
.steps5 .s h3 { font-size: 30px; margin: 8px 0 12px; }
.steps5 .s p { font: 400 21px/1.42 var(--sans); color: var(--ink-2); }
.steps5 .s .do { font: 400 20px/1.35 var(--mono); color: var(--ink); background: var(--paper-2); padding: 10px 12px; margin: 12px 0 0; word-break: break-word; }
.steps5 .s .needs { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); font: 500 19px/1.35 var(--mono); color: var(--green); letter-spacing: .02em; }
.lesson { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--hair); border-left: 10px solid var(--red); padding: 24px 30px 22px; }
.lesson h3 { font-size: 32px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.lesson p { font: 400 22px/1.42 var(--sans); color: var(--ink-2); }
.lesson p.fix { margin-top: 10px; color: var(--ink); } .lesson p.fix b { color: var(--green); }
.lesson .src { margin-top: 10px; }
.repo { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 560px 1fr 230px; gap: 24px; align-items: baseline; padding: 15px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair); }
.repo .u { font: 500 22px/1.3 var(--mono); color: var(--ink); }
.repo .w { font: 400 22px/1.38 var(--sans); color: var(--ink-2); }
.repo .l { font: 500 19px/1.3 var(--mono); color: var(--green); text-align: right; }
.anat { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--hair); border-top: 8px solid var(--green); }
.anat .row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; gap: 18px; padding: 12px 26px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair); align-items: baseline; }
.anat .row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
.anat .k { font: 500 19px/1.3 var(--mono); color: var(--ink-3); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.anat .v { font: 400 22px/1.35 var(--sans); color: var(--ink-2); } .anat .v b { color: var(--ink); }
</style></head>
<body><main class="deck">

<!-- 1 · cover -->
<section class="slide pic lightpic">
  <img class="bg" src="img/hero-diy.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:100% 50%">
  <div class="veil" style="background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(246,243,236,1) 0%,rgba(246,243,236,.96) 38%,rgba(246,243,236,.55) 50%,rgba(246,243,236,0) 60%)"></div>
  <div class="head"><span><b>Investors</b> · deck 8</span><span style="background:rgba(246,243,236,.92);padding:6px 10px;margin-top:-6px">v1.0 · 7 November 2026</span></div>
  <div class="inner" style="max-width:1040px">
    <div class="kicker">Do it yourself</div>
    <h1 style="font-size:104px">Do you want to do this yourself? <span style="color:#c52830">Fork it.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead" style="font-size:32px;max-width:900px">Everything that runs PrompTugal.news is open source: the code, the data model, the gate, the release pipeline, the agents' rules and policies. Here are the repositories, the stack, the roadmap and the lessons. Go and do it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span style="background:rgba(246,243,236,.9);padding:6px 10px">Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 2 · the invitation -->
<section class="slide v ink">
  <div class="head"><span><b>The invitation</b></span><span>02</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Dinis Cruz, founder and CTO, 7 November 2026</div>
  <p class="bigquote" style="font-size:68px">"The moat here is execution: setting this thing up and making it work. This is easy to copy. Will somebody copy? Here's the roadmap, go and do it."</p>
  <div class="cols c3" style="margin-top:70px;gap:40px">
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">1 · IT IS OPEN</div><p>Code under Apache-2.0, text and data under CC BY 4.0. No part is held back.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">2 · THIS IS THE MAP</div><p>The stack, the ten steps in order, what each takes, and where each file lives.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">3 · THE HARD PART IS YOURS</div><p>A team, a structure, a vision, and somebody who is going to do it, every day.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 3 · what is open -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>What is open</b></span><span>03</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">The repositories and packages, all public</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:64px">Five places to start. Nothing behind a login.</h2>
  <div style="margin-top:30px;border-top:3px solid #121317">
    <div class="repo"><span class="u">github.com/PrompTugal/<br>PrompTugal__News__Website</span><span class="w"><b style="color:#121317">This site, whole:</b> the build, the gate, CI, the data and its schemas, the agents' board, keys and policies.</span><span class="l">APACHE-2.0 CODE<br>CC BY 4.0 TEXT</span></div>
    <div class="repo"><span class="u">github.com/PrompTugal/<br>PrompTugal__App__iOS</span><span class="w">The iPhone and iPad app (v0.3.1, internal beta).</span><span class="l">OPEN SOURCE</span></div>
    <div class="repo"><span class="u">github.com/SGit-AI/<br>SGit-AI__Website__Web-Summit</span><span class="w">The Web Summit team's site: where the release and tag scripts came from, its agents and its investor section.</span><span class="l">OPEN SOURCE</span></div>
    <div class="repo"><span class="u">pip install sgit-ai<br>pip install sharness-ai</span><span class="w"><b style="color:#121317">sgit:</b> encrypted vaults, agent keypairs, append lanes. <b style="color:#121317">SHarness:</b> RiskMandate's secure harness.</span><span class="l">APACHE-2.0</span></div>
    <div class="repo" style="border-bottom:0"><span class="u">newsroom.sgit.ai<br>open-source.sgit.ai</span><span class="w">The first newsroom (the reading meter and the vault), and the strategy: why everything is open.</span><span class="l">PUBLIC</span></div>
  </div>
  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:30px;margin-top:34px">
    <div class="stat"><div class="v" style="font-size:72px">426</div><div class="l">releases since the first commit, 4 Nov 2026</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="v" style="font-size:72px">31</div><div class="l">signed articles, every fact sourced</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="v" style="font-size:72px">120</div><div class="l">companies with sourced profiles</div></div>
    <div class="stat r"><div class="v" style="font-size:72px">~25</div><div class="l">named agent roles, one human operator</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">Counted from github.com/PrompTugal/PrompTugal__News__Website, 7 Nov 2026; roles from its CLAUDE.md. Licences: the repository's LICENSE; sgit.ai; riskmandate.ai/secure-harness.html.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 4 · the stack -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>The stack</b></span><span>04</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Eight layers, from the facts up to the person who decides</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:54px;max-width:1680px">Each layer is a folder you can read. No server sees the readers.</h2>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 1680 650" width="1680" height="650" style="margin-top:28px">
    <g font-size="24">
      <!-- 8 human -->
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="1680" height="74" fill="#121317"/>
      <text x="26" y="47" class="serif" font-size="30" font-weight="600" fill="#f6f3ec">The human editor</text>
      <text x="470" y="46" fill="#c8c4ba">the only one who instructs; decides what is theirs alone</text>
      <text x="1654" y="46" text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#8fd18f">/newsroom/decisions/</text>
      <!-- 7 agents -->
      <rect x="0" y="82" width="1680" height="74" fill="#e2eedf"/>
      <text x="26" y="129" class="serif" font-size="30" font-weight="600" fill="#006600">Agents and their policies</text>
      <text x="470" y="128" fill="#3f424a">one role each, one written grant each, deny by default</text>
      <text x="1654" y="128" text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#121317">board/team/ · board/abp/</text>
      <!-- 6 keys -->
      <rect x="0" y="164" width="1680" height="74" fill="#e2eedf" opacity=".6"/>
      <text x="26" y="211" class="serif" font-size="30" font-weight="600" fill="#006600">sgit keys and lanes</text>
      <text x="470" y="210" fill="#3f424a">a key per agent session; sealed, write-only inboxes</text>
      <text x="1654" y="210" text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#121317">board/keys.json · board/inboxes/</text>
      <!-- 5 vault -->
      <rect x="0" y="246" width="1680" height="74" fill="#fffdf8" stroke="#1f4fa8" stroke-width="3"/>
      <text x="26" y="293" class="serif" font-size="30" font-weight="600" fill="#1f4fa8">The reader's vault</text>
      <text x="470" y="292" fill="#3f424a">encrypted in the browser; the server stores what it cannot read</text>
      <text x="1654" y="292" text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#121317">assets/ · sgit vaults</text>
      <!-- 4 hosting -->
      <rect x="0" y="328" width="1680" height="74" fill="#ece7db"/>
      <text x="26" y="375" class="serif" font-size="30" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">Static hosting</text>
      <text x="470" y="374" fill="#3f424a">plain files on GitHub Pages; no back end for readers, no tracking</text>
      <text x="1654" y="374" text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#121317">CNAME · Pages</text>
      <!-- 3 CI -->
      <rect x="0" y="410" width="1680" height="74" fill="#ece7db"/>
      <text x="26" y="457" class="serif" font-size="30" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">CI that owns the version</text>
      <text x="470" y="456" fill="#3f424a">gate, number, build, gate again, tag, deploy, check the live site</text>
      <text x="1654" y="456" text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#121317">.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml</text>
      <!-- 2 build -->
      <rect x="0" y="492" width="1680" height="74" fill="#ece7db"/>
      <text x="26" y="539" class="serif" font-size="30" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">The build and the gate</text>
      <text x="470" y="538" fill="#3f424a">Node only, no dependencies; one file per section of the site</text>
      <text x="1654" y="538" text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#121317">newsroom/build/</text>
      <!-- 1 data -->
      <rect x="0" y="574" width="1680" height="74" fill="#121317" opacity=".08"/>
      <rect x="0" y="574" width="10" height="74" fill="#c52830"/>
      <text x="26" y="621" class="serif" font-size="30" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">Data and the graph</text>
      <text x="470" y="620" fill="#3f424a">a folder per entity, a schema per file, a source and date per fact</text>
      <text x="1654" y="620" text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#121317">data/ · content/</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <div class="src">From the repository: CLAUDE.md, newsroom/build/README.md, data/README.md, board/abp/README.md, .github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml; sgit.ai ("the server that stores it cannot read it").</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 5 · the machine -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>The machine</b></span><span>05</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">From a fact to a live page, with nobody writing a version number</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:64px">Write the source. The gate and CI do the rest.</h2>
  <div class="flow" style="margin-top:34px">
    <div class="step"><div class="n">1</div><h3>Source</h3><p>Prose in <code>content/</code>, facts as JSON in <code>data/</code>, each file checked against its schema.</p></div>
    <div class="step"><div class="n">2</div><h3>Build</h3><p><code>build.mjs</code>: load, pages, decorate, fill, write, API, agent surface.</p></div>
    <div class="step"><div class="n">3</div><h3>Gate</h3><p><code>validate.js</code> builds once and must print OK. A red gate never leaves your machine.</p></div>
    <div class="step"><div class="n">4</div><h3>Release</h3><p><code>release.sh</code> rebases on <code>dev</code>, runs the gate, pushes, waits for the live site.</p></div>
    <div class="step" style="border:3px solid #006600"><div class="n">5</div><h3>CI</h3><p>Gate, number vX.Y.Z, build, gate again, commit, tag, deploy to Pages.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div style="margin-top:30px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px 20px;flex-wrap:wrap">
    <span style="font:500 20px/1 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;color:#595c64;margin-right:6px">EVERY BUILD WRITES</span>
    <span class="tag">a markdown twin per page</span><span class="tag">llms.txt</span><span class="tag">JSON API /api/v1/</span><span class="tag k">SHA-256 manifest</span>
  </div>
  <div class="cols" style="margin-top:20px;gap:40px">
    <div class="card g" style="padding:26px 30px"><div class="n">TO ADD A SECTION</div><p>One file, <code>newsroom/build/features/&lt;name&gt;.mjs</code>: its pages, its API, its search entries, its own checks for the gate. The core never changes.</p></div>
    <div class="card r" style="padding:26px 30px"><div class="n">THE RULE THAT SAVES YOU</div><p>Generated output is never committed. Edit <code>content/</code>, <code>data/</code> and <code>assets/</code>; the gate refuses an unsigned article and stale derived data.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">newsroom/build/README.md; newsroom/tools/release.sh; .github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml; newsroom.sgit.ai/articles/ci-owns-the-version.html.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 6 · an agent, taken apart -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>An agent, taken apart</b></span><span>06</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">What every one of the roles has, in files you can copy</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:58px;max-width:1680px">An agent is a name, a key, a written mandate and a record.</h2>
  <div class="cols" style="grid-template-columns:1.05fr 1fr;gap:56px;margin-top:36px">
    <div class="anat">
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Name</span><span class="v"><b>role@PrompTugal.dinis</b>; workers dotted: <b>dev.search@</b></span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Key</span><span class="v">its own session key; public half in <code>board/keys.json</code></span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Role</span><span class="v"><code>ROLE.md</code>: focus, paths, done when, never</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Policy</span><span class="v">a grant: paths, hosts, tools. All else denied</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Budget</span><span class="v">tokens and runs per day, per pass: <code>board/budgets.json</code></span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Inbox</span><span class="v">a sealed append lane: <code>board/inboxes/&lt;role&gt;.json</code></span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">State</span><span class="v"><code>status.json</code>: done, next, asks for the human</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Record</span><span class="v">a run report per run; a hand-over debrief per day</span></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 style="font-size:34px;margin-bottom:18px">How the policies hold</h3>
      <ol class="co" style="list-style:none;counter-reset:co">
        <li style="font:400 23px/1.42 var(--sans);color:#3f424a;margin-bottom:20px"><b style="display:block;font:600 27px/1.25 var(--serif);color:#121317">1 · Re-anchored, not remembered</b>A hook prints the agent's own policy back at every start and after every compaction.</li>
        <li style="font:400 23px/1.42 var(--sans);color:#3f424a;margin-bottom:20px"><b style="display:block;font:600 27px/1.25 var(--serif);color:#121317">2 · Hooks in observe mode</b>Every tool call outside the grant is logged. "Blocking should always be the last worst case scenario" (Dinis).</li>
        <li style="font:400 23px/1.42 var(--sans);color:#3f424a;margin-bottom:20px"><b style="display:block;font:600 27px/1.25 var(--serif);color:#121317">3 · The record, reviewed hourly</b>Policies tighten; relaxations go to the human to decide.</li>
      </ol>
      <div style="border-left:8px solid #1f4fa8;padding:6px 0 6px 24px;margin-top:8px">
        <p style="font:400 22px/1.42 var(--sans);color:#3f424a">After RiskMandate's Agent Behaviour Policy: <b style="color:#121317">reach</b> (measured), <b style="color:#121317">mandate</b> (authorised), <b style="color:#121317">gap</b> (derived). It "defines the mandate and measures the gap; it does not enforce it."</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">CLAUDE.md; board/abp/README.md (and what the hooks cannot see); board/the-team-setup.md; riskmandate.ai/abp.html, read 7 Nov 2026.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 7 · the roadmap, as a flow -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>The roadmap</b></span><span>07</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Ten steps, in the order we would do them again</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:64px">Foundation, machine, team, edition.</h2>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 1680 620" width="1680" height="620" style="margin-top:30px">
    <defs><marker id="ar" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" viewBox="0 0 14 14" markerWidth="22" markerHeight="22" refX="10" refY="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L14,7 L0,14 z" fill="#121317"/></marker></defs>
    <!-- phase bands -->
    <rect x="0" y="0" width="1000" height="44" fill="#e2eedf"/><text x="20" y="31" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#006600" letter-spacing="2">FOUNDATION · 1 TO 3</text>
    <rect x="1010" y="0" width="670" height="44" fill="#e3e9f5"/><text x="1030" y="31" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#1f4fa8" letter-spacing="2">THE MACHINE · 4 TO 6</text>
    <rect x="0" y="326" width="1000" height="44" fill="#f8e4df"/><text x="20" y="357" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#c52830" letter-spacing="2">THE TEAM · 7 TO 9</text>
    <rect x="1010" y="326" width="670" height="44" fill="#121317"/><text x="1030" y="357" class="mono" font-size="20" fill="#f6f3ec" letter-spacing="2">THE EDITION · 10</text>
    <!-- row 1 path -->
    <line x1="130" y1="140" x2="1550" y2="140" stroke="#121317" stroke-width="4"/>
    <path d="M1550,140 C1680,140 1680,466 1550,466" fill="none" stroke="#121317" stroke-width="4"/>
    <line x1="1550" y1="466" x2="140" y2="466" stroke="#121317" stroke-width="4"/>
    <g text-anchor="middle">
      <circle cx="130" cy="140" r="40" fill="#006600"/><text x="130" y="154" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">1</text>
      <text x="130" y="220" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">Fork</text><text x="130" y="252" class="mono" font-size="19" fill="#595c64">the repository</text>
      <circle cx="460" cy="140" r="40" fill="#006600"/><text x="460" y="154" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">2</text>
      <text x="460" y="220" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">Keys</text><text x="460" y="252" class="mono" font-size="19" fill="#595c64">one per agent</text>
      <circle cx="790" cy="140" r="40" fill="#006600"/><text x="790" y="154" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">3</text>
      <text x="790" y="220" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">A policy each</text><text x="790" y="252" class="mono" font-size="19" fill="#595c64">deny by default</text>
      <circle cx="1120" cy="140" r="40" fill="#1f4fa8"/><text x="1120" y="154" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">4</text>
      <text x="1120" y="220" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">Your data</text><text x="1120" y="252" class="mono" font-size="19" fill="#595c64">your beat, sourced</text>
      <circle cx="1450" cy="140" r="40" fill="#1f4fa8"/><text x="1450" y="154" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">5</text>
      <text x="1450" y="220" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">Build and gate</text><text x="1450" y="252" class="mono" font-size="19" fill="#595c64">must print OK</text>
      <circle cx="1450" cy="466" r="40" fill="#1f4fa8"/><text x="1450" y="480" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">6</text>
      <text x="1450" y="546" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">CI</text><text x="1450" y="578" class="mono" font-size="19" fill="#595c64">owns the version</text>
      <circle cx="1120" cy="466" r="40" fill="#c52830"/><text x="1120" y="480" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">7</text>
      <text x="1120" y="546" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">The first agents</text><text x="1120" y="578" class="mono" font-size="19" fill="#595c64">conductor, journalist, dev</text>
      <circle cx="790" cy="466" r="40" fill="#c52830"/><text x="790" y="480" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">8</text>
      <text x="790" y="546" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">Hourly wakes</text><text x="790" y="578" class="mono" font-size="19" fill="#595c64">one scheduled task each</text>
      <circle cx="460" cy="466" r="40" fill="#c52830"/><text x="460" y="480" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">9</text>
      <text x="460" y="546" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">The human who decides</text><text x="460" y="578" class="mono" font-size="19" fill="#595c64">decisions as pages</text>
      <circle cx="130" cy="466" r="48" fill="#121317"/><text x="130" y="482" class="serif" font-size="42" font-weight="600" fill="#f6f3ec">10</text>
      <text x="130" y="554" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">First edition</text><text x="130" y="586" class="mono" font-size="19" fill="#595c64">one event, in public</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 8 · steps 1 to 5 -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>The roadmap · 1 to 5</b></span><span>08</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Foundation and machine: what to do, and what each takes</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:58px">Make it yours before any agent touches it.</h2>
  <div class="steps5">
    <div class="s"><div class="n">1</div><h3>Fork</h3><p>Keep the licences. Rewrite <code>CLAUDE.md</code> for your publication: its name, its human, its rules.</p><div class="do">git clone; node 18+</div><div class="needs">TAKES: NODE ONLY, NO DEPENDENCIES</div></div>
    <div class="s"><div class="n">2</div><h3>Keys</h3><p>Each agent session makes its own key. The public half goes in <code>board/keys.json</code>; the private half never in the repository.</p><div class="do">pki-agent.mjs keygen --session</div><div class="needs">TAKES: SGIT, PKI.SGIT.AI</div></div>
    <div class="s"><div class="n">3</div><h3>A policy each</h3><p>One grant per agent in <code>policies.json</code>: paths, hosts, tools. Start strict, in observe mode.</p><div class="do">node board/abp/tools/abp.mjs build</div><div class="needs">TAKES: THE HOOKS IN .CLAUDE/</div></div>
    <div class="s c"><div class="n">4</div><h3>Your data</h3><p>Replace our companies and events with your beat: a folder per entity, a schema per file, a source URL and date per fact.</p><div class="do">data/&lt;type&gt;/&lt;slug&gt;/</div><div class="needs">TAKES: PUBLIC FACTS ONLY</div></div>
    <div class="s c"><div class="n">5</div><h3>Build and gate</h3><p>Build locally; the gate must print OK. New sections as features, never in the core.</p><div class="do">node newsroom/build/validate.js</div><div class="needs">TAKES: ONE FILE PER FEATURE</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">CLAUDE.md (Identity; Build and gate; Content); board/abp/README.md; data/README.md; newsroom/build/README.md. Key tool: https://pki.sgit.ai/agents/pki-agent.mjs.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 9 · steps 6 to 10 -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>The roadmap · 6 to 10</b></span><span>09</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Team and edition: what to do, and what each takes</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:58px">Then give it a team, a rhythm and a boss.</h2>
  <div class="steps5">
    <div class="s c"><div class="n">6</div><h3>CI</h3><p>Copy the workflow. It gates, numbers, tags and deploys; everyone releases with one script, nobody writes a version.</p><div class="do">AGENT=you newsroom/tools/release.sh</div><div class="needs">TAKES: GITHUB PAGES, A DOMAIN</div></div>
    <div class="s r"><div class="n">7</div><h3>The first agents</h3><p>Three roles, three sessions: the conductor plans and routes, the journalist writes and signs, dev owns the build.</p><div class="do">board/team/&lt;role&gt;/ROLE.md</div><div class="needs">TAKES: ONE SESSION PER ROLE</div></div>
    <div class="s r"><div class="n">8</div><h3>Hourly wakes</h3><p>A scheduled task per agent, on its own minute. At each wake: pull, read, work, release, status, commit.</p><div class="do">board/schedule.json</div><div class="needs">TAKES: A HOLD SWITCH: HOLD.MD</div></div>
    <div class="s r"><div class="n">9</div><h3>The human who decides</h3><p>Decisions are pages with every option in full. Asks start with your name. Only you instruct.</p><div class="do">/newsroom/decisions/</div><div class="needs">TAKES: SOMEONE, EVERY DAY</div></div>
    <div class="s k"><div class="n">10</div><h3>Your first edition</h3><p>One event or one beat. Signed, sourced articles; a front page; ship, then fix it in the next push.</p><div class="do">content/articles/&lt;slug&gt;.md</div><div class="needs">TAKES: A REASON TO EXIST</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">CLAUDE.md (Hourly runs; Decisions are pages; When in doubt, push to production; Branches and versions); board/the-team-setup.md; board/schedule.json.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 10 · one wake -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>The rhythm</b></span><span>10</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">What every agent does, every hour</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:62px">One wake, eight moves. Then the next agent's minute.</h2>
  <div class="cols" style="grid-template-columns:780px 1fr;gap:40px;margin-top:26px;align-items:center">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 780 640" width="780" height="640">
      <defs><marker id="cw" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" viewBox="0 0 14 14" markerWidth="20" markerHeight="20" refX="7" refY="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L14,7 L0,14 z" fill="#006600"/></marker></defs>
      <circle cx="360" cy="320" r="232" fill="none" stroke="#d9d2c1" stroke-width="4"/>
      <path d="M360,88 A232,232 0 1 1 196,156" fill="none" stroke="#006600" stroke-width="5" stroke-dasharray="12 10" marker-end="url(#cw)"/>
      <circle cx="360" cy="320" r="108" fill="#121317"/>
      <text x="360" y="306" text-anchor="middle" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#f6f3ec">every</text>
      <text x="360" y="352" text-anchor="middle" class="serif" font-size="40" font-weight="600" fill="#8fd18f">hour</text>
      <g font-size="22" font-weight="600" fill="#121317">
        <circle cx="360" cy="88" r="26" fill="#006600"/><text x="360" y="96" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" class="serif" font-size="26">1</text><text x="400" y="46">Pull dev</text>
        <circle cx="524" cy="156" r="26" fill="#c52830"/><text x="524" y="164" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" class="serif" font-size="26">2</text><text x="560" y="140">HOLD.md?</text><text x="560" y="166" font-weight="400" font-size="19" class="mono" fill="#c52830">then stop</text>
        <circle cx="592" cy="320" r="26" fill="#006600"/><text x="592" y="328" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" class="serif" font-size="26">3</text><text x="632" y="300">Read the</text><text x="632" y="326">rules</text>
        <circle cx="524" cy="484" r="26" fill="#006600"/><text x="524" y="492" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" class="serif" font-size="26">4</text><text x="562" y="532">Drain inbox</text>
        <circle cx="360" cy="552" r="26" fill="#006600"/><text x="360" y="560" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" class="serif" font-size="26">5</text><text x="360" y="614" text-anchor="middle">Do the next piece</text>
        <circle cx="196" cy="484" r="26" fill="#006600"/><text x="196" y="492" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" class="serif" font-size="26">6</text><text x="40" y="540">Release it</text>
        <circle cx="128" cy="320" r="26" fill="#006600"/><text x="128" y="328" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" class="serif" font-size="26">7</text><text x="0" y="276">status.json</text>
        <circle cx="196" cy="156" r="26" fill="#006600"/><text x="196" y="164" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" class="serif" font-size="26">8</text><text x="10" y="92">Commit: done,</text><text x="10" y="118">and what blocks</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <div>
      <div class="card g" style="padding:24px 30px;margin-bottom:22px"><div class="n">PASSES</div><p>Focused rounds on one thing, in a fixed order, within a budget: conductor, security, reviews, designer and dev, security, a note, conductor. A pass never loops on its own findings.</p></div>
      <div class="card c" style="padding:24px 30px;margin-bottom:22px"><div class="n">DECISIONS ARE PAGES</div><p>The owner proposes, reviewers weigh in on the page, the owner decides and ships. Only money, the law, the brand and people wait for the human.</p></div>
      <div class="card r" style="padding:24px 30px"><div class="n">NEVER BLOCKED IN SILENCE</div><p>A blocked agent writes an ask that starts with the human's name, and says it first when spoken to.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 11 · what you will hit -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>What you will hit</b></span><span>11</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Lessons we paid for in the first three days, from the agents' own debriefs</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:58px">None of it is the code. All of it is running the thing.</h2>
  <div class="cols" style="gap:28px;margin-top:30px">
    <div class="lesson"><h3>Agents blocked by their environment</h3><p>Every agent got an inbox; reading it needed a package the sessions were not allowed to install. Each wrote its block to another agent, so the human was not told for hours.</p><p class="fix"><b>Now:</b> the setup script installs it; every ask starts "Dinis:"; one list every agent reads.</p><div class="src">board/team/librarian/bug-2026-11-06-agents-blocked.md</div></div>
    <div class="lesson"><h3>Names changed four times</h3><p>The Lisbon Wire, then PrompTugal, then PromptUGAL for a few hours, then PrompTugal.news; and <code>admin/</code> became <code>newsroom/</code>, every agent's name with it.</p><p class="fix"><b>Now:</b> one move, by one agent, in one commit; no redirects while there are no readers.</p><div class="src">content/newsroom/decisions/the-story-of-the-name.md; board/the-newsroom-move.md</div></div>
    <div class="lesson"><h3>Keys die with sessions</h3><p>A session's private key lives only in its container. Restart it and the key, and anything sealed only to it, is gone. sgit itself says it has no rotation workflow yet.</p><p class="fix"><b>Now:</b> each new session makes a key and marks the old one superseded; a daily debrief carries what it learnt.</p><div class="src">board/team/customers/debriefs/2026-11-06-handover.md; board/team/backup/debriefs/2026-11-06-handover.md</div></div>
    <div class="lesson"><h3>Conflicts when many agents push</h3><p>Everyone appends to the same key list; a rebase replays a thousand commits; GitHub Pages refuses a deploy while another is in progress.</p><p class="fix"><b>Now:</b> the release script merges key lists by id; workers merge, never rebase; CI retries and checks the live site.</p><div class="src">newsroom/tools/release.sh; board/team/dev.data/debriefs/2026-11-07-handover.md; deploy-pages.yml</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>Do it yourself</span></div>
</section>

